+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow ref pinning
+
+Remote actions and reusable workflows can be required to use release versions or immutable commit SHAs. This opt-in check covers
+both step-level action references and job-level reusable workflow references:
+
+```yaml
+jobs:
+  call:
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/test.yml@v1.2.3
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: owner/action@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
+```
+
+Configure the minimum required level in [`actionlint.yaml`](config.md#action-pinning):
+
+- `major-minor` accepts `vMAJOR.MINOR`, full semantic versions, and full commit SHAs.
+- `semver` accepts `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (including prereleases) and full commit SHAs. This is the default.
+- `commit-sha` accepts only a full 40-character lowercase hexadecimal commit SHA.
+
+Local references starting with `./` and Docker references starting with `docker://` are not checked. A reference whose action or
+workflow name is an expression is also skipped. An expression used only as the ref is reported because its pinning cannot be
+verified statically. For known popular actions, diagnostics include a specific known action version.
+
+The error kind reported by this rule is `action-pinning`. Diagnostics identify whether the reference is a step action or a
+reusable workflow.
+
 <a id="check-local-action-inputs"></a>
 ## Local action inputs validation at `with:`
 
